 "proof", "parent_tag": "05XZ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0005": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0006": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0007": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0008": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0009": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0010": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0011": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$W \\to Z$", "MATH_0002": "$U'$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\sigma \\in F(U')$", "MATH_0005": "$\\sigma$", "MATH_0006": "$\\sigma$", "MATH_0007": "$\\sigma$", "MATH_0008": "$Z_\\sigma = \\sigma(Z_{U'}) \\subset W_{U'}$", "MATH_0009": "$Z_\\sigma \\to Z_{U'}$", "MATH_0010": "$Z_\\sigma \\to U'$", "MATH_0011": "$$\nF \\longrightarrow (W/U)_{fin}, \\quad\n\\sigma \\longmapsto (U' \\to U, Z_\\sigma)\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$(W/U)_{fin}$", "MATH_0013": "$W \\to U$", "MATH_0014": "$\\sigma$", "MATH_0015": "$Z_\\sigma$", "MATH_0016": "$Z_\\sigma \\to Z_{U'}$", "MATH_0017": "$(W/U)_{fin}$", "MATH_0018": "$U$", "MATH_0019": "$F \\to (W/U)_{fin}$", "MATH_0020": "$U' \\to U$", "MATH_0021": "$Z' \\subset W_{U'}$", "MATH_0022": "$Z' \\to U'$", "MATH_0023": "$U'' \\subset U'$", "MATH_0024": "$T \\to U'$", "MATH_0025": "$U''$", "MATH_0026": "$Z' \\times_{U'} T$", "MATH_0027": "$Z \\times_{U'} T$", "MATH_0028": "$Z \\to B$", "MATH_0029": "$W \\to Z$", "MATH_0030": "$W'$", "MATH_0031": "$W' \\to W$", "MATH_0032": "$W' \\to W$", "MATH_0033": "$W \\to Z$", "MATH_0034": "$F'$", "MATH_0035": "$W' \\to Z \\to U$", "MATH_0036": "$F'$", "MATH_0037": "$U$", "MATH_0038": "$F' \\to F$", "MATH_0039": "$\\Sch/U$", "MATH_0040": "$U'$", "MATH_0041": "$\\sigma : Z_{U'} \\to W_{U'}$", "MATH_0042": "$\\xi \\in F(U')$", "MATH_0043": "$$\nF'' = F' \\times_{F, \\xi} U'\n$$", "MATH_0044": "$\\Sch/U'$", "MATH_0045": "$$\nW'_{U'} \\times_{W_{U'}, \\sigma} Z_{U'} \\to Z_{U'} \\to U'.\n$$", "MATH_0046": "$F''$", "MATH_0047": "$U'$", "MATH_0048": "$F' \\to F$", "MATH_0049": "$F$", "MATH_0050": "$F' \\to F$", "MATH_0051": "$F \\to U$", "MATH_0052": "$F' \\to U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-section-immersion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-properties-lemma-etale-permanence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-etale-universally-injective-open}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-more-groupoids-section-finite}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-more-groupoids-proposition-finite-algebraic-space}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-where-isomorphism}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-surjection-space-of-sections}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{bootstrap-theorem-final-bootstrap}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e796f9007ba5f0cb4d6e87f05bf9c72b1118b5baf4f6dac9d3f7c9e2c436e052", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5b1cae0a0087586719a56c4be7056e30bf72dfd39317d2754daff1c3dcc196bd", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nAssume first that <MATH_0001> is also separated.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a scheme over <MATH_0003> and let <MATH_0004>. By\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe morphism <MATH_0005> is a closed immersion.\nMoreover, <MATH_0006> is <ACCENT_0001>tale by\nProperties of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nHence <MATH_0007> is also an open immersion, see\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nIn other words, <MATH_0008> is\nan open subspace such that the morphism <MATH_0009>\nis an isomorphism. In particular, the morphism <MATH_0010>\nis finite. Hence we obtain a transformation of functors\n<MATH_0011>\nwhere <MATH_0012> is the finite part of the morphism <MATH_0013>\nintroduced in\nMore on Groupoids in Spaces, Section\n<REF_0004>.\nIt is clear that this transformation of functors is injective (since we can\nrecover <MATH_0014> from <MATH_0015> as the inverse of the isomorphism\n<MATH_0016>). By\nMore on Groupoids in Spaces, Proposition\n<REF_0005>\nwe know that <MATH_0017> is an algebraic space <ACCENT_0002>tale over <MATH_0018>.\nHence to finish the proof in this case it suffices to show that\n<MATH_0019> is representable and an open immersion.\nTo see this suppose that we are given a morphism of schemes <MATH_0020>\nand an open subspace <MATH_0021> such that <MATH_0022>\nis finite. Then it suffices to show that there exists an\nopen subscheme <MATH_0023> such that a morphism\n<MATH_0024> factors through <MATH_0025> if and only if <MATH_0026>\nmaps isomorphically to <MATH_0027>. This follows from\nMore on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0006>\n(here we use that <MATH_0028> is flat and locally of finite presentation\nas well as finite).\nHence we have proved the lemma in case <MATH_0029> is separated\nas well as <ACCENT_0003>tale.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nIn the general case we choose a separated scheme <MATH_0030> and a surjective\n<ACCENT_0004>tale morphism <MATH_0031>. Note that the morphisms <MATH_0032> and\n<MATH_0033> are separated as their source is separated. Denote <MATH_0034> the\nfunctor associated to <MATH_0035> as in the lemma. In the first\nparagraph of the proof we showed that <MATH_0036> is representable by an\nalgebraic space <ACCENT_0005>tale over <MATH_0037>. By\nLemma <REF_0007>\nthe map of functors <MATH_0038> is surjective for the <ACCENT_0006>tale topology\non <MATH_0039>. Moreover, if <MATH_0040> and <MATH_0041>\ndefine a point <MATH_0042>, then the fibre product\n<MATH_0043>\nis the functor on <MATH_0044> associated to the morphisms\n<MATH_0045>\nSince the first morphism is separated as a base change of a separated\nmorphism, we see that <MATH_0046> is an algebraic space <ACCENT_0007>tale over <MATH_0047>\nby the result of the first paragraph. It follows that <MATH_0048> is a\nsurjective <ACCENT_0008>tale transformation of functors, which is representable\nby algebraic spaces. Hence <MATH_0049> is an algebraic space by\nBootstrap, Theorem <REF_0008>.\nSince <MATH_0050> is an <ACCENT_0009>tale surjective morphism of algebraic spaces\nit follows that <MATH_0051> is <ACCENT_0010>tale because <MATH_0052> is <ACCENT_0011>tale.\n<STRUCT_0004>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:48e9c6d0fdb8885fef9044d68e8711905fc67e444327e3fea62fc99dcd107654", "unit_id": "inventory:criteria:05XR:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:criteria:inventory:criteria:05Y0:paragraph/0001", "hash": "sha256:b2444f2a1fbabee46050d38dc487e7fb8dbcb12199e971cc879dfeeec19f6243", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 49618, "byte_start": 49495, "file": "criteria.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:dfbc42da45b421c9f93f50c70945bebb914f480787f0de5ff1cbcd68527f865c", "line_end": 1262, "line_start": 1260}, "owner_tag": "05Y0", "parent_tag": "05Y0", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05Y0", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-section-relative-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ab55cf9a9cf4b3194210d83e71db23bf1112f0c9dccaab255cfdecf3481ceba9", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe continue the discussion started in\nMore on Morphisms, Section <REF_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:74b509f7c8780729d8fd499a070ae20bd6e937bfae439b7106fff9255f390cd5", "unit_id": "inventory:criteria:05Y0:paragraph/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-reference:bootstrap:inventory:bootstrap:04S6:theorem/0001:bootstrap-theorem-final-bootstrap", "hash": "sha256:290d97af1ffb2b4730b40e53717579805ba95ca4f11b3bb1f5872d84935ec334", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 53058, "byte_start": 51655, "file": "bootstrap.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:e5a8664a963